[TEXT] Now the full picture is clear. The VRRP layout reveals **per-VLAN active/standby load-balancing** across the DSW pairs. Let me map it out:

| VLAN | Site A Master | Site A Backup | Site B Master | Site B Backup |
|------|-------------|--------------|---------------|--------------|
| VLAN10 | **dswa1** ✅ relay | dswa2 ❌ | **dswb1** ✅ relay | dswb2 ❌ |
| VLAN20 | **dswa2** ❌ NO relay | dswa1 ✅ | **dswb2** ❌ NO relay | dswb1 ✅ |
| VLAN30/40 | **dswa2** ❌ NO relay | dswa1 ✅ | **dswb2** ❌ NO relay | dswb1 ✅ |

The VRRP masters for VLAN20/30/40 — dswa2 and dswb2 — are the ones **without** dhcrelay. Let me confirm the DHCP server identity and whether it's actually receiving relayed requests, then enter the matching fault family skill:
