[TEXT] Both dswa2 and dswb2 can **reach** the DHCP server at 10.0.0.76 — routing is not the problem. The fault is purely the missing relay daemon.

The VRRP layout confirms the impact scope: dswa2 is the active VRRP master for VLAN20 (10.2.0.0/24) and VLAN40 (10.6.0.0/24); dswb2 is the active VRRP master for VLAN20 (10.4.0.0/24) and VLAN30 (10.5.0.0/24). Those VLANs' DHCP relay path is completely broken because their active L3 gateway has no relay agent. This maps squarely to the `dhcp-fault-skill` family.
